# onnxruntime-node (a transitive dep of @huggingface/transformers) ships its CPU
# binary in-package and only DOWNLOADS its optional CUDA/GPU execution-provider
# binary on install — a large, flaky GitHub download that fails CI with ECONNRESET.
# We only ever use onnxruntime-web inside the browser embedding iframe (ADR-109),
# so skip that download entirely. npm exports this as npm_config_* to the install
# script, which honours it in CI (`npm ci`), local installs, and the release build.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
